{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Staircase"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.canonicalScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.canonicalScale","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StaircaseCornerHook.lean#L185-L193","doc":"The canonical scale `q^(1/(2k-1))` on the base ring, realised via the\nexternal `canonicalScaleAxiom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.canonicalScaleAxiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.canonicalScaleAxiom","kind":"opaque","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StaircaseCornerHook.lean#L170-L183","doc":"The abstract canonical scale function `q^(1/(2k-1))` — meaningful in any\nring `R` admitting a `(2k-1)`-th root structure.  Specialise to\n`Real.rpow q (1 / (2k-1))` over `R = ℝ`.\n\n`opaque`, not `axiom`, and no longer called \"…Axiom\": this **names a constant\nwith an unspecified value; it asserts nothing**. An `axiom` producing *data*\nstill lands in `#print axioms` for every downstream result, which buries the\naxioms that are genuine assumptions among ones that are merely unspecified\nconstants — and the `Axiom` suffix invited reading it as a claim about the\nscale, which it never was. The value is `0`; it is hidden behind `opaque`, so\nnothing downstream can unfold it and no consumer gains a fact from it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.StaircaseEWResidual.spectral_scale_present","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.StaircaseEWResidual.spectral_scale_present","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StaircaseCornerHook.lean#L157-L157","doc":"For every `k ≥ 2`, the inverse-corner-hook scale `scale k`\n(intended interpretation: `q ^ (1 / (2k − 1))`) is realised as\na ratio of two positive eigenvalues of the canonical staircase\nβ_EW operator on `V_{ρ k}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.StaircaseEWResidual.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.StaircaseEWResidual.mk","kind":"ctor","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StaircaseCornerHook.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.StaircaseEWResidual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.StaircaseEWResidual","kind":"class","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StaircaseCornerHook.lean#L145-L158","doc":"Axiomatic class encoding the staircase EW-residual conjecture. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:staircase-ew-residual","label":"conj:staircase-ew-residual","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/staircase-ew-residual.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.StaircaseEWSpectralContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.StaircaseEWSpectralContent","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StaircaseCornerHook.lean#L117-L143","doc":"Concrete spectral statement: in any Hoefsmit representation `HR`\nof `H_{n_k}(q)` on the staircase Specht module `V_{ρ k}`, the\nmatrix image of the canonical β_EW Δ_I^minimal word has two\nnonzero eigenvalues whose ratio is `q ^ (1 / (2k - 1))`.\n\nThe exponent `1 / (2k - 1)` lives in the real / `rpow` world; we\nstate the predicate over an arbitrary `R` together with a\ndesignated **scale element** `s : R` standing for the would-be\n`q ^ (1 / (2k - 1))`.  Downstream callers supply `s` either by\nworking over `ℝ` with `Real.rpow`, or by adjoining a `(2k−1)`-th\nroot of `q` to the base ring.\n\nThis replaces the previous opaque\n`axiom StaircaseEWSpectralContent (k : ℕ) : Prop` with a\npredicate that actually mentions the Hoefsmit-matrix spectrum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.staircase_corner_hook_eq_two_k_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.staircase_corner_hook_eq_two_k_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StaircaseCornerHook.lean#L55-L70","doc":"**Provable lemma.** The corner hook of the staircase `ρ k` equals\n`2*k - 1` for every `k ≥ 1`.\n\nThis is purely combinatorial: it follows from the definition of the\nstaircase shape and the hook-length formula, with no appeal to\nrepresentation theory or any spectral data.\n\nRef: [stanley1999] Enumerative Combinatorics II, §7.21\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:staircase-corner-hook","label":"lem:staircase-corner-hook","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/staircase-corner-hook.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.hCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StaircaseCornerHook.hCorner","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StaircaseCornerHook.lean#L42-L53","doc":"The corner hook of the staircase `ρ k = (k, k-1, …, 1)` at cell\n`(0, 0)`.  Defined directly as the combinatorial quantity:\n\n  `h_corner k := arm(0,0) + leg(0,0) + 1`\n\nFor the staircase `ρ k`:\n\n* `arm(0,0) = (length of row 0) - 1 = k - 1`\n* `leg(0,0) = (number of rows with ρ k r ≥ 1) - 1 = k - 1`\n\nso `h_corner k = (k - 1) + (k - 1) + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}